WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.820
Most of the time when you go to the movies,
you can expect the story you see on the big

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.069
screen to be resolved by the time the lights
come up.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:13.110
Maybe not all the good guys will make it to
the end, but for the most part the world will

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.840
be as it should be.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.900
But not every story can have a happy ending.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.369
Sometimes the price of victory is high, and
characters we learned to love are taken away

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:23.369
from us.

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:27.240
Other times the heroes don't win at all, no
matter how much they sacrificed.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.800
Man on Fire may not have been a favorite of
critics, but Denzel Washington's performance

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.940
as alcoholic bodyguard John Creasy was one
of the most moving of his career.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.530
After years of booze and bullets, Creasy gets
a shot at redemption as a bodyguard for Pita,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.019
played by Dakota Fanning.

00:00:45.019 --> 00:00:50.359
When a powerful crime syndicate captures Pita,
Creasy buys pretty much every gun in Mexico

00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:54.859
and goes on a murder spree, eventually capturing
the kidnapper's brother.

00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:59.969
Dying from a gunshot wound, Creasy trades
himself for the safety of his charge.

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:05.100
But before handing himself over, he reunites
with Pita for just a few seconds.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.409
When he tells her goodbye, it's a moment that
will make even the toughest action fan weep.

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:13.409
"Where are you going?"

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:18.100
"I'm goin' home, too."

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.799
While the boxing drama Million Dollar Baby
may at times feel as inspirational as Rocky,

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:28.560
Rocky Balboa never ended a movie quite like
this.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.890
Hilary Swank plays Maggie Fitzgerald, a backwoods
waitress hoping to make her name as a boxer,

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:37.630
and director Clint Eastwood plays grizzled
trainer Frankie Dunn.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:43.640
Dunn is reluctant to teach a woman at first,
especially one as old as Maggie, but eventually

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.719
her persistence wins him over.

00:01:45.719 --> 00:01:50.280
Maggie proves her worth, KOing her way to
a championship fight, and that's when the

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.149
movie takes a hard left turn.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:58.140
Maggie is paralyzed from the neck down when
her opponent illegally punches her after the

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.140
bell.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.220
Our hero falls hard from the punch, smashing
her neck against a footstool.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.580
Maggie loses her leg, and she begs her trainer
to end her suffering.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:14.190
Dunn refuses at first, but agrees after Maggie
tries and fails to commit suicide.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:20.410
Before Dunn administers the lethal injection,
he tells Maggie the meaning of her Irish nickname.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:29.080
"'Mo Cuishle' means 'my darling, my blood.'"

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:34.200
Even steely-eyed Eastwood can't keep the tears
back here, and you know if even Dirty Harry

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.040
is getting weepy, there's no way you're going
to be able to hold it back.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:45.020
"Niagara Falls, Frankie Angel."

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:51.120
After the tragic death of bear-enthusiast
Timothy Treadwell at the jaws of a brown bear,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.370
director Werner Herzog assembled Treadwell's
footage and created Grizzly Man, one of the

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.200
most moving documentaries of all time.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.220
Grizzly Man follows Treadwell as he journeys
into the Alaskan wilderness, interacts with

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.989
animals, and shares his unique view about
man's place in nature.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:13.049
While Treadwell's behavior is sometimes questionable,
it's hard not to admire his passion.

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:17.560
With the help of Herzog's guiding hand, we
grow attached to Treadwell as Grizzly Man

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.190
heads for its inevitable tragic ending.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:24.920
While we go into Grizzly Man knowing Treadwell's
fate, it's upsetting to finally say goodbye

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.590
to such a unique soul.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:31.569
In the film's last moments, we watch for the
last time as Treadwell wanders into the woods,

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:36.560
accompanied by two fuzzy friends and a mournful
country song that feels like it was written

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.560
just for him.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:42.700
While Wes Anderson directs comedies, there's
always a deep sense of melancholy underlying

00:03:42.709 --> 00:03:43.709
his work.

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:47.040
That's especially true for The Grand Budapest
Hotel.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:53.000
Set in the fictional European country of Zubrowka,
the film's narrative is nestled inside multiple

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.650
timelines, with the bulk of it set during
the 1930s.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:02.560
Our hero Zero Moustafa played by both Tony
Revolori and F. Murray Abraham, works as a

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:09.540
lobby boy at the Grand Budapest Hotel under
the guidance of flamboyant concierge M. Gustave,

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.370
played by Ralph Fiennes.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:16.570
The plot involves a dead heiress, a missing
painting, and a family of greedy goons, but

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:21.070
the drama revolves around the dark shadow
hanging over this dreamworld.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:26.440
In the 1930s, the hotel is an impossibly charming
world of pastel colors.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:32.720
As the story continues, both Zubrowka and
Grand Budapest are overrun by enemy forces,

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.570
quasi-Nazis followed by quasi-Soviets.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:41.280
As the totalitarian horrors of the 20th century
creep in, M. Gustave's civilized world starts

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.280
to fade.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.720
Guests stop coming and eventually the building
is torn down.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:52.410
M. Gustave is killed during the war, communism
washes over Zubrowka, and Zero is left alone

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.170
with nothing but his memories of better days.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:59.850
The film ends with the nostalgic author saying
over the closing frame, "It was an enchanting

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.820
old ruin, but I never managed to see it again."

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:08.600
On its cold, gray surface, The Blackcoat's
Daughter is a movie about a girl who's demonically

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:09.610
possessed.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:14.600
But under the slow-building dread and eerie
music, there's a tragic story about a helpless

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.040
child afraid of being alone.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.950
Played at first by Kiernan Shipka, and later
by Emma Roberts, Kat is a boarding school

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.430
student with some serious abandonment issues.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.540
When her parents are late to pick her up for
the semester break, Kat freaks out.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:33.530
It doesn't help matters any when she has an
unsettling dream about her parents' untimely

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.530
fate.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.850
Terrified her parents are dead and that she'll
be all alone in the world, Kat literally makes

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:43.740
a deal with the devil, allowing herself to
be possessed in exchange for companionship.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.380
She's so afraid of losing the spirit's company,
she beheads three people at its urging.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:54.290
When a priest exorcises the demon from Kat,
she's so scared of being alone that she begs

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.390
the beast to stay.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:59.510
Unfortunately, her pleas are no match for
holy water.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:04.430
Years later, an older Kat murders two new
victims and brings their heads back to the

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.590
school, hoping her sacrifice will summon the
demon.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:12.510
When she realizes the evil spirit has left
the school behind, the movie ends with Kat

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.370
sobbing and screaming into the wintry void.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:18.800
She realizes now that she's truly by herself.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.140
Nobody will ever come to pick her up, and
even the devil doesn't want her.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:29.800
Directed by Damien Chazelle, La La Land follows
two star-crossed lovers: Emma Stone as aspiring

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.430
actress Mia and jazz devotee Sebastian played
by Ryan Gosling.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:39.840
Mia and Sebastian enjoy the happiness and
heartache all long-term relationships face.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.490
Eventually, because of their conflicting ambitions,
they go their separate ways.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:50.090
Five years later, Mia is a movie star and
Sebastian runs a thriving nightclub.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:55.280
One night they lock eyes across a room, and
we're treated to an elaborate dream sequence.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.560
It's the kind of ending we expect to see:
the guy and girl end up with one another and

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:05.320
live happily ever after, but the dream soon
comes to an end with Mia and Sebastian once

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.790
again going their own ways.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:13.280
It's a heartbreaking reminder that the choices
we make always leave the door open for regret.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:19.400
Before Tony Stark made his Iron Man suit and
before Christian Bale donned the Bat-cowl,

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.000
there was Hugh Jackman as Wolverine.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.990
Jackman played Logan to perfection, to the
point where it seems almost impossible that

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.440
any actor could ever replace him in the role.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:35.040
He defined Wolverine for well over a decade,
appearing in every X-Men movie up until his

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.260
blood-soaked swan song, 2017's Logan.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:44.580
Set in the near-distant future, Logan follows
a dying Wolverine as he uses the last of his

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:50.260
strength to protect the young Laura who Logan
eventually learns is actually his clone.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:56.500
A shady scientist wants Laura for nefarious
purposes, and he has the vicious cybernetic

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.070
Reavers under his command.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:03.640
At first Logan is such a broken man that he
wants nothing to do with Laura, and only the

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:07.190
aging Professor X convinces him to do the
right thing.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:12.630
Unfortunately Professor X doesn't survive
the journey, but Logan continues to help Laura

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.630
all the same.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:18.470
When Laura and other mutant children try to
escape into Canada, Wolverine makes his final

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.260
stand in the woods to protect their escape.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:27.180
But even after fighting all the Reavers, Logan
still must face a clone made to be a stronger,

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.790
younger version of himself.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:33.251
With the help of Laura and her allies, the
clone is killed, but Logan's wounds are too

00:08:33.251 --> 00:08:34.610
much for him.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:39.750
Thankfully, after a brutal life full of hard
decisions, Logan enjoys a moment of fatherly

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.669
love before shuffling off this mortal coil.

00:08:42.669 --> 00:08:47.960
In the film's final scene, a tearful Laura
gives Logan the eulogy he deserves, quoting

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:51.720
Alan Ladd's final monologue from the classic
western Shane.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.370
"There's no living with the killing.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:56.140
There’s no going back.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.790
Right or wrong it’s a rat.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.560
A rat that stinks."

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.400
After ending her speech, Laura tips the cross
on his grave over on its side, marking the

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.590
Wolverine's final resting place with an X.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:13.670
While the past few years have given us plenty
of amazing superhero movies, Logan was the

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:19.120
first superhero film to truly make audiences
weep for such an iconic character.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:25.500
Since Thanos' first MCU appearance in 2012,
Marvel fans couldn't wait for the big purple

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.190
baddie to throw down with the Avengers.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:33.960
The MCU filmmakers only gave us brief, teasing
glimpses of the Mad Titan; first a little

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:39.380
bit in the initial Avengers movie, then a
lot more in Guardians of the Galaxy, and later

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.420
in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:47.360
Finally, six years after Avengers, Thanos
finally arrived with his Infinity Gauntlet,

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.360
and Earth's mightiest heroes were completely
overmatched.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.550
It looked like Thor was going to save the
day when he slammed Stormbreaker into the

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:00.170
Mad Titan's chest, but as the God of Thunder
quickly learned...

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:06.050
"You should've gone for the head."

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:11.420
And just like that, with a snap of his fingers,
Thanos wiped out half the population of the

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:14.620
universe, including the majority of our beloved
heroes.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:20.000
Along with most of the Avengers turning to
dust, almost all the Guardians fell victim

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.900
to Thanos' purge.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:27.300
Rocket was there to watch Teenage Groot fade
away, and to hear his final "I Am Groot."

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:32.050
Adding to the sorrow of many fans, Guardians
of the Galaxy's writer and director James

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:37.750
Gunn would eventually reveal that Groot's
last "I am Groot" translated into the word,

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:38.750
"Dad."

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:42.830
For many fans, Peter Parker's death was the
most painful to watch.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:48.150
Even though he just fought the toughest villain
in the MCU, Peter's still just a kid, afraid

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.320
of fading away.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:53.670
Considering we know many of the characters
that died at the end of Infinity War have

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:59.980
more solo films in their respective franchises
planned, it seems pretty likely Avengers 4

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.190
will undo a lot of Thanos' damage.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:07.230
Still, you know things are bad when Captain
America, the team's most optimistic member,

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.740
is unable to do anything but whisper...

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:17.160
"Oh God."

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:21.820
Infinity War might have the darkest ending
of any major blockbuster ever.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.760
There's no moral victory; no feel good speech.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:30.340
For the first time, the Avengers have truly
lost, and it all ends with Thanos admiring

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:35.670
his handiwork, smiling as the sun rises on
a "grateful universe."

